Rule 1 (dim indexes a valid axis of y)
{v_1 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= (ndim(v_1) ≥ 1) ∧ (-1 × ndim(v_1) ≤ v_3) ∧ (v_3 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1)
>>
Rule 2 (x provides one coordinate per sample point along dim)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= 0 ≤ v_3 ∧ v_3 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1 ∧ ((ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) = shape(v_1, v_3)) ∨ (ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_1) ∧ shape(v_2, v_3) = shape(v_1, v_3)))
>>
Rule 3 (y and x must not be boolean tensors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0) ∧ (dtype_(v_2) ≠ 0)
